
  <sn><md>### Possible Pitfall Due to Trigraphs

**Version:** ≥ C99

When writing `//` delimited comments, it is possible to make a `typographical error` that affects their expected behavior. Consider the following example:

```c
int x = 20;
// Why did I do this??/
```

The `/` at the end was a typo, but now it will be interpreted as `\`. This happens because the sequence `??/` forms a **trigraph**.

The `??/` trigraph is a **longhand notation** for the backslash character `\`, which serves as the **line continuation symbol** in C. This means the compiler treats the next line as a continuation of the current line — in this case, as a continuation of the comment. This may not be what the programmer intended.
</md></sn>
