<sn><md>#### Example of unintended behavior:

```c
int foo = 20; // Start at 20 ??/
int bar = 0;
// The following line will cause a compilation error (undeclared variable 'bar')
// because 'int bar = 0;' is actually part of the comment on the preceding line
bar += foo;
```

In the code above, the `??/` trigraph causes the comment to extend onto the next line, effectively commenting out `int bar = 0;`. As a result, `bar` is never declared, leading to a compilation error when trying to use it.</md></sn>